  "id": "DrugBank_DB00352 - MONDO_15165",
  "verbalization": "Tioguanine appears to be associated with Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) and Myelodysplastic Syndromes (MDS) related to Topoisomerase Type 2 inhibitors through a series of indication links. The evidence suggests that Tioguanine is linked to AML and MDS through its use in treating Mitoxantrone, which in turn is indicated for these conditions. This implies a potential pathway where Tioguanine may have a role in the treatment of AML and MDS, possibly through a mechanism that involves the inhibition of Topoisomerase Type 2 enzymes. The overlapping indications across different paths suggest a possible shared therapeutic or pathophysiological role, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a relationship between Tioguanine and these conditions, but further research is needed to elucidate the precise mechanism of action and its relevance to the disease.",
